            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for to write to each other, then the Mandarin for phone charges."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: guàduàn",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "guàduàn — \"to hang up the phone; to end a call\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tā hái méi shuō wán jiù guàduàn le diànhuà — He hung up before he had finished."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "guàduàn is built from guà 'to hang' and duàn 'to cut off', both inherited from Middle Chinese, kweaH and dwanX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to suspend' and the second 'to sever'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
